Z||000005||GREENDANO||04-18-2000||07:05 AM||||That picture is from an IRM catalog.  The price is each and GOOD LUCK getting them.  After some serious health problems with the husband  (IRM is a husband wife business)  their customer service went out the door.  Maybe it's improved since this January, anyone?....  I had my car dead on jack stands for an extra month waiting for my braided brake hoses, finally got a hold of a real person, cancelled my order, ordered a set from the Fiero Store and had them in two days.<BR>  I do like the wheels though, I want a set for my F40.<BR>  Dan-O ||||reg||1
Z||000006||1FST2M6||04-18-2000||08:44 AM||||Konig wheels are cheap... don't shoot your self down till you actully call!  I paid $150 each for my 17x7.5 Konig GT-Rs. the Rushes are about the same price.. (17x7-42mm offset) <A HREF="http://www.discounttiredirect.com" TARGET=_blank>www.discounttiredirect.com</A>   the Compo- rims are SWEET. their almost as light as Panasports! (of comperable size and width) But if your gunna drop $285 each I'd look at Dymag, HRE, or Fikse. there is a 928 at the shop with Fikse wheels .. they were $320 each.. 17x12 (rear) 17x9.5 (front) ||||reg||1
